+# TLS Backend
+
+The project's current recorded decision is to use rustls as its TLS backend. It was chosen because it is a pure Rust implementation of TLS, which avoids the C FFI binding layer and its maintenance complexity, and because it fits Rust's memory-safety model and ecosystem conventions.
